\text{GCD}(2002, 44444) = \text{GCD}(2002, 44444 \mod 2002) = \text{GCD}(2002, 444) = \text{GCD}(2002 \mod 444, 444) = \text{GCD}(274, 444) = \text{GCD}(274, 444 \mod 274) = \text{GCD}(274, 170) = \text{GCD}(274 \mod 170, 170) = \text{GCD}(104, 170) = \text{GCD}(104, 170 \mod 104) = \text{GCD}(104, 66) = \text{GCD}(104 \mod 66, 66) = \text{GCD}(38, 66) = \text{GCD}(38, 66 \mod 38) = \text{GCD}(38, 28) = \text{GCD}(38 \mod 28, 28) = \text{GCD}(10, 28) = \text{GCD}(10, 28 \mod 10) = \text{GCD}(10, 8) = \text{GCD}(10 \mod 8, 8) = \text{GCD}(2, 8) = \text{GCD}(2, 8 \mod 2) = \text{GCD}(2, 0) = 2 \end{aligned}
Thus, the smallest positive integer that can be written in the form $2002m + 44444n$ is $\boxed{2}$. </think> <answer> 2 </answer>

